This Java code uses the Ed25519 and BIP39 (Base 64-encoded private keys) algorithms for generating key pairs. It provides classes to generate Eds ( Edwards Curves) and Keypairs, which can be used for encrypting and decrypting data.

Please note that you need to have the necessary libraries (`bip39`, `base64`) to run this code. You can install them via Maven or Gradle if needed:

```bash
mvn install -Dbuild javax.base -DgroupId org.mkyong
```

or

```bash
gradle install
```

After installing the required libraries, you can compile and run the code using the following commands:

```bash
javac TestKeyPair.java
java TestKeyPair
